window.PC_BREEDS=[{"name":"Havanese","slug":"havanese","live_count":25,"demo_count":26,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_61fbe22101d94c70b71b39c9dd7506b3~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Great Dane","slug":"great-dane","live_count":19,"demo_count":19,"guide":["Towering in height but tender at heart, the Great Dane is one of the most majestic and lovable breeds in the dog world. Often referred to as the “Apollo of Dogs,” this giant breed combines elegance and power with a calm, affectionate nature that makes them truly special companions. Despite their commanding presence, Great Danes are known for being sweet, loyal, and surprisingly gentle.","Great Danes are truly awe-inspiring in stature, standing 28 to 34 inches tall and often weighing between 110 to 175 pounds. Their sleek, muscular frames and long, graceful necks give them a statuesque appearance, while their short, smooth coats come in a variety of colors and patterns—including fawn, brindle, harlequin, black, mantle, and blue.","But perhaps their most captivating feature is their expression: alert, kind, and intelligent, with eyes that reflect their calm and loyal spirit. Their noble looks turn heads wherever they go, but it’s their gentle personality that truly wins hearts.","Don’t let their size fool you—Great Danes are among the most affectionate and people-loving breeds around. They thrive on companionship and often see themselves as lap dogs (despite their size!). These gentle giants are known for being incredibly loyal, good-natured, and patient, especially with children and other pets.","Great Danes are typically calm indoors and enjoy being part of the family’s daily life. They’re not overly energetic, but they do need regular exercise and mental engagement. Most importantly, they crave closeness with their humans and are happiest when included in the household routine.","Great Danes make excellent family dogs thanks to their friendly, steady temperament and deep devotion to their people. They are especially good with children, often showing remarkable gentleness and patience. Their size does require some supervision around smaller kids, but their sweet nature makes them loving and protective playmates."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_9e03dab4eb674dd591e3084e05046e3e~mv2.jpeg"},{"name":"Miniature Poodle","slug":"miniature-poodle","live_count":21,"demo_count":18,"guide":["The Miniature Poodle: Elegance, Intelligence, and Charm in One Delightful Package","Graceful, clever, and full of personality, the Miniature Poodle is the perfect blend of beauty and brains. Often seen in show rings with their signature haircuts, Poodles are so much more than just pretty faces—they're athletic, eager to please, and deeply bonded to their families. The Miniature variety, in particular, offers the perfect in-between size: small enough for apartment life, but sturdy enough for active play and adventure.","Miniature Poodles are beautifully proportioned, standing about 10 to 15 inches tall and weighing between 10 and 15 pounds. Their coats are curly, dense, and low-shedding—making them a popular choice for allergy-conscious families. These coats come in a wide range of solid colors including white, black, apricot, red, cream, silver, blue, and more.","While many recognize the show-style grooming, Poodles can also be kept in lower-maintenance clips for everyday life. With regular grooming and brushing, they stay looking polished and stylish—perfect for a dog that naturally carries itself with a touch of flair.","Miniature Poodles are among the smartest of all dog breeds. They’re quick learners who thrive on mental stimulation and love a good challenge. Whether it’s mastering obedience, learning tricks, or trying out agility or rally, the Miniature Poodle is always up for it.","But they’re not just smart—they’re incredibly loving, too. Poodles form strong bonds with their people and love to be near them. They’re attentive, affectionate, and often sensitive to their owner’s mood, making them excellent companions for those looking for a dog that truly connects."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_13e0ecb960dd47099023d9fd2758b1d8~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Cavalier King Charles Spaniel","slug":"cavalier-king-charles-spaniel","live_count":24,"demo_count":17,"guide":["Few breeds embody charm and affection quite like the Cavalier King Charles Spaniel. With their graceful appearance and endlessly loving nature, these small yet sturdy toy dogs have enchanted pet owners for centuries. Whether curled up in your lap or trotting happily at your side, Cavaliers make devoted companions who thrive on human connection.","Cavaliers boast a silky, medium-length coat that flows elegantly as they move, with signature feathering on their ears, chest, legs, and tail. Their expressive, round eyes are perhaps their most captivating feature, radiating warmth and an ever-present eagerness to please. Despite their royal lineage, Cavaliers are anything but aloof—one wag of their feathery tail is enough to show just how friendly and affectionate they truly are.","Cavaliers are often described as “Velcro dogs” because of their deep devotion to their owners. They crave companionship and are happiest when they can be by your side, whether that means snuggling on the couch or following you from room to room. Their gentle and friendly nature makes them excellent therapy dogs, and their adaptability allows them to fit into a wide range of lifestyles.","While they are not known for being stubborn, Cavaliers are sensitive dogs who respond best to positive reinforcement. They aim to please and thrive on love, making them relatively easy to train. However, they do not do well when left alone for long periods—these social butterflies need plenty of interaction to stay happy.","One of the greatest qualities of the Cavalier King Charles Spaniel is their adaptability. They can thrive in both active households and quieter settings, adjusting their energy levels to match their owner’s lifestyle. They are wonderful companions for families with children, as well as ideal pets for seniors looking for a devoted and affectionate friend.","Cavaliers generally get along well with other dogs and even cats, making them a great choice for multi-pet households. Their friendly, non-aggressive nature means they welcome new people with open paws, making them poor guard dogs but excellent social companions."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_c27316f4fcfb480d99ecba235b5dbf95~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Cavapoo","slug":"cavapoo","live_count":17,"demo_count":17,"guide":["The Cavapoo, a delightful mix of the Cavalier King Charles Spaniel and the Poodle, has quickly become one of the most beloved designer breeds. With their affectionate nature, intelligence, and irresistibly fluffy appearance, these charming dogs make wonderful companions for a variety of lifestyles. Whether you’re looking for a playful friend or a cuddly lap dog, the Cavapoo offers the best of both worlds.","Cavapoos inherit their soft, wavy, or curly coats from their Poodle parent, making them both adorable and low-shedding—an excellent choice for allergy-sensitive owners. They come in a variety of colors, including cream, apricot, red, black, and even parti-color combinations. Their round, expressive eyes and button noses give them a forever-puppy look that melts hearts instantly.","Thanks to their small to medium size, typically ranging from 9 to 14 inches tall and weighing between 10 to 25 pounds, Cavapoos are adaptable dogs that fit comfortably into homes of all sizes, from apartments to large houses with yards.","Cavapoos are incredibly affectionate and thrive on human interaction. They are known for their loving and social nature, making them excellent companions for families, singles, and seniors alike. With their Cavalier side bringing warmth and their Poodle lineage contributing intelligence, Cavapoos are both gentle and highly trainable.","These dogs are people-oriented and love to be the center of attention. They enjoy playtime, walks, and mental stimulation but are just as happy curling up next to you for a cozy cuddle session. Their adaptable temperament makes them great companions for both active and laid-back lifestyles.","Cavapoos are excellent with children and other pets, making them a fantastic addition to families. Their gentle and patient nature means they get along well with kids, while their playful energy makes them a fun-loving playmate. They are also friendly toward strangers, so while they may not be the best guard dogs, they will greet guests with wagging tails and enthusiastic affection."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_581802288ecc434fb451d36d290ce8ea~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Miniature Schnauzer","slug":"miniature-schnauzer","live_count":15,"demo_count":15,"guide":["Charming, spirited, and brimming with personality, the Miniature Schnauzer is a small dog with a big heart and even bigger character. Known for their iconic beards and expressive eyebrows, these sturdy little terriers are alert, affectionate, and endlessly entertaining. Whether they’re patrolling the yard or snuggling on the couch, Miniature Schnauzers are true companions—loyal to their people and always ready for fun.","The Miniature Schnauzer is easily recognized by their distinguished appearance: a wiry double coat, bushy brows, and that trademark beard that gives them an almost human-like expression. Standing 12 to 14 inches tall and weighing around 11 to 20 pounds, they’re the smallest of the Schnauzer breeds but have the confidence and presence of a much larger dog.","They come in several classic color combinations—salt and pepper, black and silver, and solid black—each adding to their bold and classy look. Regular grooming keeps their coat in top condition and brings out their sharp, tidy silhouette.","Miniature Schnauzers are intelligent and eager to please, which makes them a joy to train. They learn quickly, love mental challenges, and excel in obedience, tricks, and even dog sports like agility or rally. Their terrier background gives them a bit of a mischievous streak, but it’s all part of their lively charm.","These dogs are known for their cheerful nature and strong bond with their families. They’re affectionate without being clingy, and they love being involved in daily life—whether that means going for a walk, playing in the yard, or just keeping an eye on everything from their favorite perch.","Miniature Schnauzers are wonderful with children and make excellent family pets. They’re playful, patient, and protective, and usually get along well with other dogs and pets, especially when socialized early. Their alert nature also makes them excellent watchdogs—they’ll let you know if someone’s at the door, but they’re not typically yappy when well-trained."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_ce1a9f29e32e4e1c82141a0513bec0fe~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Munchkin Bernedoodle","slug":"munchkin-bernedoodle","live_count":13,"demo_count":11,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_4af6aa74d73e4654b60a8a5b134e55c9~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Golden Retriever","slug":"golden-retriever","live_count":11,"demo_count":11,"guide":["Few breeds are as universally beloved as the Golden Retriever. With their shining golden coats, soulful eyes, and famously friendly personalities, Goldens have earned their place as one of the most popular family dogs in the world. Loyal, intelligent, and endlessly affectionate, Golden Retrievers are more than just beautiful—they’re true-hearted companions who bring happiness wherever they go.","Golden Retrievers are known for their luscious double coats, which range from pale cream to rich gold. Their kind, intelligent expressions and feathered tails that seem to wag with joy are signature features of the breed. Medium to large in size—typically 21 to 24 inches tall and 55 to 75 pounds—Goldens are both sturdy and graceful.","Golden Retrievers are famously friendly and eager to please. They bond deeply with their people and have a natural love for just about everyone—kids, adults, other dogs, and even strangers. This makes them poor guard dogs, but exceptional family pets.","Their intelligence and willingness to learn make them one of the easiest breeds to train. They thrive on positive reinforcement and love having a job to do, whether it's fetching a ball, mastering new tricks, or helping with therapy work. They’re gentle, patient, and wonderfully intuitive—an ideal match for both active families and individuals seeking a loyal best friend.","Golden Retrievers are incredibly adaptable and truly shine in family environments. They are gentle with children, friendly with guests, and usually get along great with other pets. Goldens are happiest when they’re included in family activities and given plenty of affection and attention.","Because they are people-oriented, they don’t like to be left alone for long periods. If they get lonely or bored, they may turn to chewing or digging for entertainment—so regular interaction and stimulation are key to keeping them happy."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_65294cadf97d4635b7dc0b0223c3e934~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Shih Tzu","slug":"shih-tzu","live_count":10,"demo_count":10,"guide":["Bred for royalty and raised to adore their humans, the Shih Tzu is a lapdog through and through—with a personality that’s both sweet and spirited. With their flowing coats, short snouts, and bright, expressive eyes, Shih Tzus have been charming their way into hearts for centuries. These little lions might be small in stature, but they carry themselves with grace, humor, and undeniable charm.","The Shih Tzu’s long, silky coat is one of its signature features—flowing to the floor in full show coat or neatly trimmed for a more casual look. Available in a rainbow of colors, from gold and white to black, brindle, and everything in between, their glamorous appearance is only matched by their delightful disposition.","Weighing in around 9 to 16 pounds and standing about 9 to 10.5 inches tall, Shih Tzus are compact and sturdy, with a distinctive pushed-in face, a proud, arched neck, and a plumed tail that curls over their back. Whether lounging on a velvet pillow or trotting around the house, they carry themselves like royalty.","Shih Tzus are known for their affectionate and friendly nature. They love people—especially their own family—and thrive on attention and companionship. While they’re happy to curl up in your lap for hours, they’re also playful and full of personality, often surprising you with silly antics and little spurts of zoomies.","They get along well with children, other dogs, and even cats, making them a great choice for families or multi-pet households. Though they can be a bit stubborn at times (as all royalty can be), they’re so endearing that you can’t help but laugh and go along with their quirks.","Shih Tzus are ideal companions for those living in apartments, condos, or smaller homes. They don’t need a ton of exercise—just some daily play and a few short walks to stay happy and healthy. They’re indoor dogs at heart and prefer lounging in the air conditioning over romping around in the heat."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_10a86db25b5f450f84714872642d6780~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Mini Aussiedoodle","slug":"mini-aussiedoodle","live_count":9,"demo_count":9,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_0fb8c1e786d84839a1fb836110ce855c~mv2.jpeg"},{"name":"Mini Bernedoodle","slug":"mini-bernedoodle","live_count":8,"demo_count":8,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_77a8387dfb194922931120dfb170fefb~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Toy Poodle","slug":"toy-poodle","live_count":5,"demo_count":5,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_ea200d5e536c4653b7ce828aa8e29b80~mv2.jpeg"},{"name":"F1b Mini Goldendoodle","slug":"f1b-mini-goldendoodle","live_count":5,"demo_count":5,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_c5a8581a83984262a7896186bc9f39e4~mv2.jpeg"},{"name":"Pembroke Welsh Corgi","slug":"pembroke-welsh-corgi","live_count":9,"demo_count":4,"guide":["Short in stature but huge in personality, the Pembroke Welsh Corgi is one of the most beloved breeds in the world—and for good reason. Famous for their fox-like faces, perky ears, and wiggly little tails (or lack thereof!), these sturdy herders are full of spunk, smarts, and heart. Known for being Queen Elizabeth II’s favorite breed, the Pembroke Corgi has earned its royal reputation both on palace grounds and in family homes everywhere.","Pembroke Welsh Corgis are instantly recognizable with their long bodies, short legs, and bright, intelligent expressions. Weighing between 25 and 30 pounds and standing about 10 to 12 inches tall, they’re a compact breed that’s surprisingly athletic and agile.","Their thick double coats come in colors like red, sable, fawn, and tri-color, often paired with white markings. While they do shed (especially during seasonal changes), regular brushing helps keep their coats healthy and manageable. And yes, those signature butts are just as adorable in real life as they are on the internet!","Corgis were originally bred to herd cattle, and that working-dog intelligence and drive are still alive and well in the breed today. They’re quick learners who love to be challenged, and they often excel in obedience, agility, and even tricks.","Beyond their brains, Pembrokes are famously affectionate and loyal. They adore being part of the family and have a strong desire to be involved in whatever their people are doing. Whether it's tagging along on errands or keeping you company while you relax, Corgis are always close by, ready for action—or a belly rub.","Pembroke Welsh Corgis make fantastic family pets. They tend to be great with children, playful without being overwhelming, and social with other dogs and even cats (with the right introductions). They’re naturally watchful and protective, making them excellent watchdogs who are quick to alert you—but not typically excessive barkers when properly trained."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_ad055603447a427ba06f1c3fbd3c7242~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Miniature Dachshund","slug":"miniature-dachshund","live_count":6,"demo_count":4,"guide":["With their unmistakable long bodies, short legs, and lively eyes, Miniature Dachshunds are full of charm and character. Often affectionately called \"wiener dogs\" or \"doxies,\" these tiny hounds pack a bold personality into a petite frame. Originally bred to hunt badgers, today’s Miniature Dachshund is just as courageous—but far more likely to be found curled up on a cozy blanket or keeping their humans entertained with their spunky antics.","Miniature Dachshunds are instantly recognizable. Their long torsos, stubby legs, and deep chests give them a distinctive silhouette that’s both quirky and endearing. Despite their small size—typically weighing under 11 pounds—they carry themselves with surprising confidence.","They come in three coat varieties: smooth, long-haired, and wire-haired, each with its own special charm. Colors and patterns abound, from classic red and black-and-tan to dapple, piebald, and more. Whatever their look, Miniature Dachshunds have a way of drawing smiles wherever they go.","Mini Dachshunds may be small, but their personalities are anything but. These little dogs are lively, brave, and curious. They’re incredibly loyal to their families and often form strong bonds with one or two favorite humans. Despite their lap-sized stature, they have a big-dog attitude and aren’t afraid to speak their minds.","While their independent streak can sometimes translate into a bit of stubbornness, their cleverness and love for treats make them fun to train. They love being involved in family activities and won’t hesitate to let you know when they want attention or playtime.","Miniature Dachshunds are adaptable and do well in both apartments and houses, as long as they have cozy places to nap and space to explore. They’re wonderful companions for individuals and families alike, and they usually get along well with older children who understand how to handle them gently."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_f6eeab9128fd411681adafc0eea4ba15~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Boston Terrier","slug":"boston-terrier","live_count":5,"demo_count":4,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_2bd1c6e821cc4389aebdd19985372f0f~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Teddy Bear (Shihchon)","slug":"teddy-bear-shihchon","live_count":4,"demo_count":4,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_9fe3ab982d2d4334ad0564464b831c5a~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Victorian Bulldog","slug":"victorian-bulldog","live_count":4,"demo_count":3,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_5ed1d981810b4b4d9a28a8c067b2d638~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Doberman Pinscher","slug":"doberman-pinscher","live_count":3,"demo_count":3,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_8a6b8ae6400d49f38c597986438d4cae~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Pomeranian","slug":"pomeranian","live_count":9,"demo_count":2,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_c1315bc8884240c8ada7218ae31ef0a1~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Yorkshire Terrier","slug":"yorkshire-terrier","live_count":4,"demo_count":2,"guide":["Don’t let the petite size fool you—Yorkshire Terriers (or “Yorkies”) pack a ton of personality into their small frames. Known for their silky coats, sparkly eyes, and spirited nature, Yorkies are one of the most popular toy breeds in the world. They’re bold, affectionate, and always ready to strut their stuff. Whether nestled in a designer bag or confidently leading the way on a walk, the Yorkie lives life with flair.","Yorkies typically weigh around 4 to 7 pounds and stand about 7 to 8 inches tall, but their presence feels much bigger. Their long, flowing coats are a signature feature—often steel blue and tan in color, soft as silk, and full of elegance. Many Yorkie owners choose to keep the coat trimmed short for easy maintenance, though those growing it out for show know how much pride (and brushing!) comes with that stunning look.","Despite their dainty appearance, Yorkies are sturdier than they seem, full of zest and energy.","Yorkshire Terriers are fearless and feisty, with a confidence that rivals breeds ten times their size. They are smart, curious, and often act as if they rule the roost. But beneath that bold exterior is a deeply affectionate little companion who adores their people.","Yorkies love being close—preferably on your lap, tucked under your arm, or following you from room to room. They can be a bit vocal, alerting you to every passerby or unexpected sound, but their intent is always to protect their beloved humans.","Thanks to their compact size, Yorkies are perfect for apartment dwellers, urban living, or anyone with limited space. They don’t need much room to be happy, but they do need attention, love, and daily activity to burn off their energy. A brisk walk, indoor playtime, or a puzzle toy can keep your Yorkie both mentally and physically engaged."],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_88f162b1d90c4742a38b11ab538b4317~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Saint Bernard","slug":"saint-bernard","live_count":2,"demo_count":2,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_a343280cb5a1409d8efbc00c9d181680~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"Bernese Mountain Dog","slug":"bernese-mountain-dog","live_count":2,"demo_count":2,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_6e51040f9f93499696ca52d500e221e3~mv2.jpg"},{"name":"English Bulldog","slug":"english-bulldog","live_count":2,"demo_count":1,"guide":[],"photo":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8d80ac_5feb88b2d5d142fa81b67053e692d60d~mv2.jpg"}];
window.PC_BREEDERS=[{"slug":"county-line-kennel","name":"County Line Kennel","people":"Gerald and John","kennel":"County Line Kennel","body":["Gerald and John might be the most easygoing father/son team you’ll ever meet. While everyone else in the world is caught up in the rat race, these two march to a different, slower drum. Just about any given moment you’ll find John gently combing out a freshly bathed Shih Tzu, and Gerald crouching down to carefully monitor a new mom at eye-level. They share a quiet passion for dogs, and together they’ve built a canine haven that’s every bit as peaceful as they are.","John’s special gift is grooming. He has developed a stress-free approach to bath time and haircuts that the adult dogs actually enjoy! The puppies’ coats, nails, teeth, and everywhere in between are under his careful attention. Gerald enjoys getting to know the families who call about the puppies or visit their home. If a family requires transportation, Gerald and John both work closely with Furry Freight to make sure things go smoothly.","Each dog at County Line Kennel is AKC registered and receives full health exams by the vet on a regular basis, as well as daily exercise and fun outside.","John and Gerald are licensed and inspected annually by USDA, and are actively involved in the local animal welfare league. They work closely with a Kennel Management Assistance organization to constantly further their expertise.","They reserve Sundays for church and family, so  are not available for phone calls or visits on that day.","As per Indiana state law, they are required to charge sales tax for any family that comes to personally pick up their puppy."]},{"slug":"marvin-ramer","name":"Marvin Ramer","people":"Marvin","kennel":"Marvin Ramer","body":["We having been raising puppies for over 5 years now. We enjoy living on a hobby farm. I grew with animals and really enjoy the time I get to spend with my dogs. My children also love playing with our puppies and the puppies will be used to being around children.","We love our dogs and we aim to raise happy and healthy companions for your family.","Our puppies are taken to the vet for a full physical exam when they are 6 to 8  weeks of age.  We remove declaws and dock tails depending if its breed appropriate.","We do our very best to keep our dogs and puppies healthy and happy.","Vaccination Protocol - They will have their puppy deworming and vaccinations started prior to going home.","We send our puppies home with a vaccination record and a health guarantee.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"mervin-yutzy","name":"Mervin Yutzy","people":"Mervin","kennel":"Mervin Yutzy","body":["My family has been raising puppies for 5 1/2 years and we are looking forward to many more years. We have 7 children whom  give our puppies lots of quality time and attention.","We remove dewclaws as well as dock tails when it's breed is appropriate.","Our puppies will go for their first vet exam at 7 weeks.","Vaccination Protocol - Our puppies will have their dewormings and vaccations started. We give them Pyrantel, Safeguard, Ivermectin, Neo-par, 5 Way and Intractrac 3","Vaccination record, AKC papers, and sample of Eukanuba puppy food.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"perfect-match-poodles","name":"Perfect Match Poodles","people":"Perfect Match Poodles","kennel":"Gabriel and Joyce","body":["What can be more charming than a beautiful, well-bred Poodle? We love their intelligence, their affectionate dispositions, and happy attitudes. We have been specializing in Poodles since 2018 and we are committed to ensure the health and happiness of every dog and puppy. We are here to serve new puppy families for the life of the puppy. Our dogs are very much a part of our family and they love playing in the yard and playsets that we made specially for them!  Our puppies' dewclaws are removed and tails docked and they are taken to the vet for a full physical exam when they are 6-7 weeks of age. From the time our puppies are born, they receive lots of great socialization in the form of toys, playtimes with other puppies, stimulation and handling on a daily basis, and experiencing lot of different floor textures.","We are USDA and BOAH licensed and Canine Care Certified","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day.","We are required to charge sales tax for any family that comes to personally pick up their puppy.","\"We would like to thank Gabriel with Perfect Match Poodles for the most amazing Miniature Poodle puppy! Our puppy is such a good tempered and happy pup. He is doing amazing with our children. After so much searching, we were blessed to find Gabriel and Perfect Match Poodles. He was a pleasure to work with. They have a beautiful and clean kennel and play yard for their dogs. I can tell that they truly care about the pups and that they are well taken care of. I would highly recommend this breeder!\"","\"My husband and I adopted Lady a couple months ago and we could not be more overjoyed to have her in our lives! She has the best temperament, loves cuddles, and is super smart! She caught on to training very quickly. Within only a few days she was \"bell-trained\" to go outside and even learned \"sit pretty.\" We are also impressed with how great she does on our daily car rides! Gabriel and his wife are great to work with, very responsive, and they have an obvious love for all their dogs! Their facility is amazing and very clean. We are so grateful to have found our Lady!\""]},{"slug":"philip","name":"Philip","people":"Philip","kennel":"Riverdale Paw Pals","body":["On a ship you might hear, “All hands on deck!” At Riverdale Paw Pals you’d hear instead, “All paws on grass!”","When you arrive at Riverdale, the first thing you’ll notice is the yard – lush, shaded, landscaped, and most of all, played in! A yard is a wonderful thing for dogs and puppies. Every day each of our dogs gets to hunt for bugs, track scents to their hearts’ desire, run through our special doggy playground, or just lounge around in the sunshine (here’s looking at you, Basset Hounds!) The yard is also an asset in our leash training program. We value a sweet relationship with our own pets, so it's only natural to begin training good manners in our puppies as well.","Beyond socialization, at Riverdale we  prioritize health for each critter under our care, young and old alike. It’s no secret that careful breeding is the foundation for good health, so it is our goal to be known for excellence in genetics. You’ll see rows of champions in our pedigrees, but this is only part of the picture. Our adults receive breed-specific health testing, we support our moms with a top-notch diet with supplements customized to their individual needs, and each puppy receives a head-to-tail check up before joining its new family. The health guarantee we provide is a testament to our commitment to stand behind each puppy.","We have enjoyed raising dogs for 15 years. Our dream is to raise puppies that are show quality that families will love. We pay special attention to temperament to allow our adults to create a lineage that has great temperament traits. Our adults come from champion lines or show lines because we value giving you puppies with great traits. It's also important to provide quality time with our puppies and this is something we enjoy as a family.","O ver the years we have grown partial to four very special breeds: Pembroke Welsh Corgis, Cavalier King Charles Spaniels, Dachshunds, and Basset Hounds. We believe they are the best in the world, and yes, we are biased! If you also love these breeds and are searching for a new canine companion, you are welcome to visit our home to meet our dogs and puppies. We look forward to sharing our joy with you!","We remove dewclaws and our puppies are taken to the vet for a full physical exam when they are 6 weeks of age.","Vaccination Protocol - Our puppies are fully dewormed by the time they go home with a variety of dewormers recommended by our vet to prevent a wide range of parasites.","We will provide the new owner with a record of all the vaccinations and dewormings.","What we send home  -  vaccination history and puppy package.","Sales tax is applied when a family comes to personally pick up their puppy. We ask that families please dress modestly."]},{"slug":"melva","name":"Melva","people":"TM Countryside K9","kennel":"Titus and Melva","body":["Giant breeds have been a passion of ours for the past 17 years. We love the Great Dane breed with their beautiful coat colors, great temperaments, intelligence, and companionship. Occasionally we have Daniff (Great Dane/Mastiff) puppies because we love the hybrid vigor and the gentleness they bestow. Our adult dogs are vet checked regularly, have a lot of hands-on care, and are well-taken care of.  They have access to both indoors and outdoors. We take extra care to ensure that our nursing mothers are comfortable while raising their babies. The puppies are given lots of hands-on care and as they grow our family makes sure they are acclimated to various environments and experiences. At 6 weeks we start on basic training which includes crate-training, going potty outside, and walking on a leash. Before our puppies leave for their new homes, they are vet checked, microchipped, and UTD on vaccinations and dewormings. They will go to their new homes with their registration papers, health guarantee, a puppy care package, and lifetime support from us. Our goal is to provide a happy, health puppy to a fur-ever family that will keep on loving our fur-babies.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day.","We are required to charge sales tax for any family that comes to personally pick up their puppy.","I got my Great Dane puppy from Melva. She was very nice. She sent me updates every week until I picked up the puppy. The parents were on property. Everything looked really nice and well taken care of. Melva even called me to check on my puppy when I got him home. I would highly recommend them to get a puppy. Kymm, December 2021"]},{"slug":"edward-and-malinda","name":"Edward and Malinda","people":"Edward and Malinda","kennel":"Edward and Malinda","body":["Edward and Malinda Ramer have been raising 10–12 lb Miniature Dachshunds for over twelve years, focusing exclusively on this beloved breed. They live on a three-acre farmette with their five children—ranging in age from two to eleven—where puppies are raised right in the middle of busy family life.","Caring for the dogs is a shared effort. Dad handles morning chores, while Mom and the kids take care of kennel duties each evening. The children play a special role in daily puppy care, from cuddling and gentle handling to helping with early training. Their setup includes a six-pen kennel with outdoor runs and a dedicated play yard, giving puppies space to explore while remaining safely supervised.","The Ramers’ philosophy is simple and heartfelt: raise healthy, friendly, well-socialized puppies and make sure families are happy with their new companions. By specializing in only one breed and raising their females in-house for several generations, they are able to stay closely connected to their dogs’ temperaments, structure, and overall consistency.","Puppy socialization begins early. The children start holding puppies around two weeks of age and play with them every evening as they grow. When weather allows, puppies are taken outside to experience grass and fresh air; on colder or rainy days, they’re brought into the house for indoor playtime. One way this program really stands out is the introduction of collars and leashes starting at eight weeks of age, helping puppies become comfortable with basic handling and early training before they ever leave home.","Puppies are born in a kennel with heated tile flooring and remain with their mother throughout the early weeks. Around four to five weeks, they begin eating puppy food. Vaccinations are administered at five, seven, and twelve weeks of age, with deworming every two weeks beginning at three weeks. All puppies are microchipped. Veterinary care is provided by Dr. Weldy’s Associates.","Each puppy goes home with a complete vaccination and deworming record, a health certificate when required, microchip documentation, and starter food with feeding instructions.","If a Miniature Dachshund raised in a family setting—complete with early leash exposure and lots of kid love—sounds like the right fit, the Ramers are always glad to share more about their dogs and daily routine.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"tyler-and-eileen","name":"Tyler and Eileen","people":"Tyler and Eileen","kennel":"Tyler and Eileen","body":["Tyler and Eileen Martin have been raising 25–30 lb Pembroke Welsh Corgis for the past four years on their 17-acre property. They live in a ranch-style home and have thoughtfully set up a warm, comfortable space where their dogs are raised and cared for. With plenty of open pasture, their corgis have room to do what they do best—run, play, chase balls, and greet their people with enthusiasm every time they appear.","The Martins have created an environment that fits the boundless energy and curiosity of the corgi breed. Daily life includes romping in the pasture, interactive play, and plenty of human connection. The result is a group of very likeable, people-oriented dogs who enjoy both activity and attention.","Eileen has a special love for puppies and finds joy in every stage of their development. From the quiet early days to the moment they discover toys and begin bouncing from one activity to the next, she takes hands-on pleasure in watching their personalities unfold. She spends time with the puppies each morning and evening, making sure they receive consistent attention, interaction, and care.","Puppies are born in the kennel, where they are given a calm, private start to life. Socialization begins early and continues daily. When weather allows, Eileen brings the puppies outside to play in the yard; during colder months, playtime and interaction continue indoors in the kennel. Vaccinations begin after six weeks of age, and deworming is provided every two weeks.","Health testing is an important part of the Martins’ program. They regularly invest in OFA certifications for hearts, hips, elbows, and eyes to support the long-term health and soundness of their dogs.","Families who love the lively, affectionate nature of corgis and appreciate puppies raised with energy, attention, and genuine enthusiasm are invited to learn more about the Martins’ program.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"perry","name":"Perry","people":"Perry","kennel":"Perry","body":["Perry Kuhns has been dedicated to the lovely Havanese breed for over ten years at Chain-O-Lakes Kennel. He and his wife, Sharon, along with their five children, settled on their twelve-acre horse farm in LaGrange, Indiana, in 2019—a setting that allows their dogs plenty of room to grow, play, and be part of daily family life.","Caring for the dogs is truly a family effort. Perry begins each morning tending to the dogs and managing health records, vaccinations, and deworming schedules. In the evenings, the children help with chores and spend time playing with the dogs and puppies, providing valuable socialization that helps produce confident, people-loving companions.","One area where Perry especially stands out is his attention to coat type and coat care. He is intentional about breeding Havanese with correct, manageable coats and spends time maintaining them so puppies are accustomed to regular handling and grooming. This early exposure helps puppies transition more smoothly into home grooming routines and sets families up for long-term success with the breed’s signature coat.","Perry’s breeding philosophy centers on raising healthy, happy family pets. Adult dogs are OFA certified for knees, eyes, and heart, and he avoids breeding traits that could negatively impact a puppy’s quality of life. His Havanese are most commonly sable/white and black/white. He also appreciates the breed’s non-shedding, hypoallergenic coat, which makes Havanese a wonderful option for many families with allergies.","Puppies receive structured, proactive veterinary care. They are given a Neopar vaccine at four weeks, followed by Bordetella and a 5-way vaccine at five weeks. Deworming includes Pyrantel at two weeks and Fenbendazole at four, six, and eight weeks. All puppies are microchipped and are typically ready to go home at eight weeks of age. Veterinary care is provided by Alpha Vet Clinic in Shipshewana and LaGrange Vet Clinic.","Puppies are born in a climate-controlled kennel and, around six to seven weeks of age, are introduced to indoor-outdoor access through a doggie door. They are exposed to a variety of environments—including the kennel, shop, and home—helping them become comfortable with everyday sights, sounds, and activity.","Each puppy goes home with a complete vaccination and deworming record, microchip documentation, a health certificate when required, starter food, and a familiar toy and blanket from home.","Perry enjoys connecting with families who value healthy, well-raised Havanese and is always happy to answer questions about his dogs, coats, and care routines. He believes communication and transparency are important, and is glad to serve as a reference and resource for families considering one of his puppies.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"marcus-and-elaine","name":"Marcus and Elaine","people":"Marcus and Elaine","kennel":"Marcus and Elaine","body":["Marcus and Elaine Miller have been raising Miniature Schnauzers for the past eight years, with a strong focus on health, structure, and family-friendly temperaments. In early 2026, they moved to their new five-acre home, where their dogs are cared for in a dedicated 12 x 16 ft facility featuring outdoor runs and comfortable shade.","Their breeding philosophy centers on raising strong, well-balanced Miniature Schnauzers that stay true to breed standards. Marcus and Elaine intentionally focus on producing healthy dogs with bold markings, a stocky build, and the kind of temperament that makes a wonderful family companion. Their Schnauzers stay between 12-18 lbs.","building and are gradually introduced to                                                 the outdoors as they mature. The                                                                  Millers spend time with their dogs                                                                daily, especially during feeding, and                                                              puppies are gently socialized, including                                                        exposure to small children. Each puppy is microchipped and receives a 5-way vaccine at six weeks of age.","Puppies go home with a complete and accurate vaccination and deworming record, microchip registration, a health certificate when required, starter food, and a familiar toy and blanket from home. All veterinary care is provided through Alpha Vet Clinic in Shipshewana.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"cozy-pine-canine","name":"Cozy Pine Canine","people":"Cozy Pine Canine","kennel":"Cozy Pine Canine","body":["Gerald Bontrager of Cozy Pine Canine has been raising Shih Poos, Cavapoos, Poodles, and Biewer Terriers for the past nine years. He and his wife, Kayla, raise their family on a six-acre farmette where ducks, horses, puppies, and a garden full of organic food are all part of everyday life. Their two children grow up right alongside the animals, learning responsibility, kindness, and a genuine love for small critters of all kinds.","Animals are woven into the rhythm of the Bontrager household. From daily chores to quiet moments of interaction, puppies are raised in an environment where being handled, observed, and cared for is simply part of normal family life. This consistent, gentle exposure helps produce puppies that are comfortable, curious, and well-adjusted.","Gerald’s philosophy centers on raising healthy puppies for real families. He places strong emphasis on sound structure, beautiful coats, and attractive color markings, while never losing sight of what matters most—long-term health and quality of life. A key way he sets his program apart is through his commitment to genetic health. Gerald invests in comprehensive DNA panel testing, including color DNA screening, to help ensure puppies are clear of known genetic issues and to make informed breeding decisions.","Puppies are born and raised in a clean, carefully maintained environment that is washed daily and disinfected weekly. Socialization begins early, with puppies spending time outdoors in both sun and shade when weather allows. During inclement weather, puppies are kept indoors and played with on the floor, ensuring they continue to receive daily interaction and enrichment.","Vaccinations are administered at six, eight, and ten weeks of age, and dewormer is rotated every two weeks. All puppies are microchipped. Most puppies are ready to go home around ten weeks of age, though some may be ready as early as eight weeks depending on size and development. Gerald’s dogs also have their eyes certified free of disease by an OFA-affiliated ophthalmologist. Veterinary care is provided through Alpha Vet Clinic in Shipshewana.","Each puppy goes home with a complete vaccination and deworming record, a health certificate when required, microchip documentation, starter food with feeding instructions, and a familiar toy and blanket from home.","Gerald and Kayla enjoy connecting with families who value thoughtfully raised puppies and responsible breeding practices. Those interested in a puppy raised with intention, care, and a whole lot of animal love are welcome to get in touch.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]},{"slug":"maple-lane-pets","name":"Maple Lane Pets","people":"Lonnie","kennel":"Maple Lane Pets","body":["Lonnie Miller of Maple Lane Pets raises Papillons, Shih Poos, Shih Tzus, and Cavapoos on a peaceful ten-acre property, where maple trees line the drive and set the tone for daily life. Lonnie and his wife, Michelle, raise their family there with their young son, Seth, and their dogs are very much part of that rhythm.","Daily exercise and interaction are a priority. The dogs enjoy a large play yard, and little Seth is often right alongside them—playing, watching, and helping in his own way. This regular, gentle exposure to both adults and a child helps puppies grow comfortable with people and everyday activity.","Lonnie’s philosophy centers on starting with quality. He has invested in strong breeding dogs with the goal of producing healthy, happy parents—and in turn, healthy, happy puppies. Customer satisfaction matters to him, and he believes that well-cared-for adults are the foundation of good family companions.","Puppies are born in a clean, warm kennel with heated flooring and are handled and played with often by both adults and Seth. Vaccinations are administered at six, eight, and eleven weeks of age, and Lonnie works closely with his veterinarian to follow an effective deworming schedule beginning at two weeks of age.","Each puppy goes home with a complete vaccination and deworming record, a health certificate when required, starter food with feeding instructions, and a familiar toy and blanket from home.","Families looking for a puppy raised in a calm, family-centered setting—where playtime, fresh air, and daily care are part of the routine—are welcome to learn more about life at Maple Lane Pets.","We reserve Sundays for church and family, so we are not available for phone calls or visits on that day."]}];
